{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"rival-ammoniacal-crustacean","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\ntest_cli_show_complete_or_erroring_under_write_burst costs 10.95-22.63s in recent CI samples and is the largest variable default-suite node. Closed slim-fetch-ledge is the original regression and must remain protected. Closed ambery-enigmatic-pussycat later added a generic table-driven reads-under-writer-storm property but intentionally retained the original show regression byte-for-byte. Runtime overlap alone does not prove redundancy.\n\n## Plan\n- Map both tests through the CLI, store read/reconvergence, writer process, output-completeness, exit-code, timeout, and cleanup paths.\n- Enumerate the original slim-fetch-ledge failure mechanism and any failure classes only the generic property reaches.\n- Seed each defect independently and run both oracles to establish a detection matrix.\n- If the generic property misses any original behavior, keep both or strengthen it under legitimate RED-to-GREEN before considering consolidation.\n- Measure repeated macOS and Ubuntu timings and compare concurrency-regression practice in maintained OSS projects.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The original empty-or-partial-success regression remains detectable through the real CLI.\n- [ ] Fault-seeded evidence shows which oracle detects every original and generic failure class.\n- [ ] Process concurrency, output completeness, exit status, timeout, and cleanup remain real.\n- [ ] Any consolidation removes an oracle only after behavioral equivalence is proven.\n- [ ] macOS wall and aggregate runner savings are measured.\n- [ ] slim-fetch-ledge, ambery-enigmatic-pussycat, and maintained OSS precedents are cited.","id":"afa0-2e15-7db8-4d5b","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["ci","test-runtime","research","concurrency"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Prove fault-seeded equivalence before consolidating show-under-write-burst regression"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786827626453128001,"uuid":"26e735b8-c4f7-4839-a693-0c8302ff14a4"}